=== layout: one-panel

# HLA offspring

@body

- A father has a HLA genotype of A6,B4,C8 on one chromosome and A5,B7,C1 on the other.
- The mother has an HLA genotype of A8,B2,C4 on one chromosome and A3,B5,C3 on the other.
- Which one of the following is a possible HLA genotype of their offspring?
  - A. A6/A8, B2/B7, C3/C8
  - B. A5/A6, B4/B7, C1/C8
  - C. A3/A6, B4/B5, C3/C8
  - D. A6/A8, B5/B7, C4/C8

=== layout: one-panel

# HLA offspring

@body

- A father has a HLA genotype of [A6,B4,C8]{color=red} on one chromosome and [A5,B7,C1]{color=orange} on the other.
- The mother has an HLA genotype of [A8,B2,C4]{color=green} on one chromosome and [A3,B5,C3]{color=purple} on the other.
- Which one of the following is a possible HLA genotype of their offspring?
  - A. [A6]{color=red}/[A8]{color=green}, [B2]{color=green}/[B7]{color=orange}, [C3]{color=purple}/[C8]{color=red}
  - B. [A5]{color=orange}/[A6]{color=red}, [B4]{color=red}/[B7]{color=orange}, [C1]{color=orange}/[C8]{color=red}
  - C. [A3]{color=purple}/[A6]{color=red}, [B4]{color=red}/[B5]{color=purple}, [C3]{color=purple}/[C8]{color=red}
  - D. [A6]{color=red}/[A8]{color=green}, [B5]{color=purple}/[B7]{color=orange}, [C4]{color=green}/[C8]{color=red}



Keep each parent's linked A, B, and C alleles together as a haplotype.

=== layout: one-panel

# HLA offspring

@body

- A father has a HLA genotype of [A6,B4,C8]{color=red} on one chromosome and [A5,B7,C1]{color=orange} on the other.
- The mother has an HLA genotype of [A8,B2,C4]{color=green} on one chromosome and [A3,B5,C3]{color=purple} on the other.
- Which one of the following is a possible HLA genotype of their offspring?
  - A. [A6]{color=red}, [B7]{color=orange}, [C8]{color=red}/[A8, B2]{color=green}, [C3]{color=purple}
  - B. [A6, B4, C8]{color=red}/[A5, B7, C1]{color=orange}
  - C. [A6, B4, C8]{color=red}/[A3, B5, C3]{color=purple}
  - D. [A6]{color=red}, [B7]{color=orange}, [C8]{color=red}/[A8]{color=green}, [B5]{color=purple}, [C4]{color=green}



Crossing over is unlikely for adjacent genes. Eliminate A and D.

=== layout: one-panel

# HLA offspring

@body

- A father has a HLA genotype of [A6,B4,C8]{color=red} on one chromosome and [A5,B7,C1]{color=orange} on the other.
- The mother has an HLA genotype of [A8,B2,C4]{color=green} on one chromosome and [A3,B5,C3]{color=purple} on the other.
- Which one of the following is a possible HLA genotype of their offspring?
  - A. [A6]{color=red}, [B7]{color=orange}, [C8]{color=red}/[A8, B2]{color=green}, [C3]{color=purple}
  - B. [A6, B4, C8]{color=red}/[A5, B7, C1]{color=orange}
  - C. [A6, B4, C8]{color=red}/[A3, B5, C3]{color=purple}
  - D. [A6]{color=red}, [B7]{color=orange}, [C8]{color=red}/[A8]{color=green}, [B5]{color=purple}, [C4]{color=green}



One haplotype must come from each parent. Eliminate B.

=== layout: one-panel

# HLA offspring

@body

- A father has a HLA genotype of [A6,B4,C8]{color=red} on one chromosome and [A5,B7,C1]{color=orange} on the other.
- The mother has an HLA genotype of [A8,B2,C4]{color=green} on one chromosome and [A3,B5,C3]{color=purple} on the other.
- Which one of the following is a possible HLA genotype of their offspring?
  - A. [A6]{color=red}, [B7]{color=orange}, [C8]{color=red}/[A8, B2]{color=green}, [C3]{color=purple}
  - B. [A6, B4, C8]{color=red}/[A5, B7, C1]{color=orange}
  - C. [A6, B4, C8]{color=red}/[A3, B5, C3]{color=purple}
  - D. [A6]{color=red}, [B7]{color=orange}, [C8]{color=red}/[A8]{color=green}, [B5]{color=purple}, [C4]{color=green}



*Answer: C.*

=== layout: multiple-choice

@question

A mother has a HLA genotype of A7,B5 on one chromosome and A3,B3 on the other. The father has a HLA genotype of A1,B4 on one chromosome and A8,B1 on the other. Which one of the following is a possible genotype for one of their offspring?

- A. A3,A7,B3,B5
- B. A1,A7,B1,B3
- C. A3,A8,B4,B5
- D. A3,A8,B1,B3
- E. A1,A8,B1,B4

@answer

Answer: D.

=== layout: multiple-choice

@question

A mother has a HLA genotype of A6,B3,C4 on one chromosome and A9,B5,C7 on the other. The father has a HLA genotype of A8,B9,C2 on one chromosome and A2,B1,C9 on the other. Which one of the following is a possible genotype for one of their offspring?

- A. A6,A9,B3,B5,C4,C7
- B. A8,A9,B5,B9,C2,C7
- C. A2,A8,B1,B9,C2,C9
- D. A8,A9,B1,B5,C4,C9
- E. A2,A6,B5,B9,C4,C9

@answer

Answer: B.

